{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finrank","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.not_of_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.not_of_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.lean#L146-L159","doc":"**Refuted at the trivial family** — the property the old schema lacked\nentirely.\n\nFour values that are all `0` span the zero submodule, of rank `0 ≠ 2`. So the\nclass genuinely constrains the caller's `Li₃` data: a degenerate family fails\nit. Under the previous shape `⟨0, rfl⟩` closed the class for every choice of\neverything, including this one, so \"the four values realise Borel's rank\" had\nnothing to fail against. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.relations_finrank_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.relations_finrank_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.lean#L119-L139","doc":"**Exactly two independent relations** — the multiplication-formula count,\nderived rather than assumed.\n\nFour generators spanning rank `2` leave a relation space of rank `2`, by\nrank-nullity applied to `Fintype.linearCombination`. The block attributes those\nrelations to the multiplication formula; the *count* follows from the rank alone\nand needs nothing about which relations they are.\n\nThis is what makes the single field say something structural rather than merely\nnumerical. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.span_finrank_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.span_finrank_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.lean#L98-L98","doc":"**The reduced target.** The four `Li₃(ζ₅ᵏ)` span a space of rank exactly\n`2` — Borel's `dim_ℚ K₅^ind(ℚ(ζ₅)) ⊗ ℚ`.\n\nRank `2` from four generators is the whole content: it says the\nmultiplication-formula identities cut the four values down to Borel's\nrank and no further. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.mk","kind":"ctor","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5","kind":"class","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/QouInfraDischargesGoncharovZeta5.lean#L77-L99","doc":"**Goncharov's depth-3 conjecture at `ℚ(ζ₅)`, in the block's reduced form.**\n\nSee\n[`conj:qou-infra-discharges-goncharov-zeta5`](../../../appendix-surreals/qou-infra-discharges-goncharov-zeta5.md).\n\nParameters are the caller's data:\n\n* `V` — the target `ℚ`-space, standing for `𝒫₃/𝒫₂` over `ℚ(ζ₅)`;\n* `li3 k` — the value `Li₃(ζ₅^{k+1})` for `k : Fin 4`.\n\nNeither is constructed in this library, so both are supplied rather than built.\n\nAn instance **is** the conjecture, for that data. None is provided. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:qou-infra-discharges-goncharov-zeta5","label":"conj:qou-infra-discharges-goncharov-zeta5","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/qou-infra-discharges-goncharov-zeta5.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}